  "solution": {
    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0190_0113d38a5412.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 348px; height: 80px;\" /><br />menthyl <math> <mrow>  <mtext>(</mtext><mover>   <mrow>    <msub>     <mrow>      <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow>     <mtext>3</mtext>    </msub>    </mrow>   <mo>&#x2295;</mo>  </mover>  <mtext>)</mtext></mrow></math>, vinyl <math> <mrow>  <msub>   <mrow>    <mtext>(CH</mtext></mrow>   <mtext>2</mtext>  </msub>  <mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>=</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mover>   <mrow>    <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow>   <mtext>+</mtext>  </mover>  <mtext>)</mtext></mrow></math>. Among the given options benzyl is highly stabilised by resonance and so is allylic but lesser than benzyl. Vinylic has a <math> <mrow>  <msup>   <mrow>    <mtext>sp</mtext></mrow>   <mtext>2</mtext>  </msup>  </mrow></math> carbocation which is unstable in nature."
